# The default stub: steps 1 to 19, and step 20 stopping the arm exactly as it stops
# `--model-forward`. Section 6, correction C6 records why the availability gate keeps R5B's code.
#
# This list is deliberately **five** rows and not R5B's twenty-seven. Steps 1 to 19 are the *same*
# `model_forward.execute` on both arms — section 3.1's whole point — and the block above this one
# already drives every one of those rules through it. What is unproven until it runs here is that
# the new arm reaches that path at all, with its own operand grammar and its own document kind, and
# one row per operand class settles it. Re-running twenty-seven identical validations against
# identical code would cost `make layer-forward-smoke` about two seconds and assert nothing the
